# Support UTF-8 fused adapters over shared memory, including memory64.
#
# RISC Box's shared wasm64 module uses a wasm32 WASI compatibility component.
# FACT must preserve the shared memory's declared maximum. Its UTF-8 helper
# snapshots bytes atomically, validates owned data, then atomically publishes
# it, so no Rust slice borrows concurrently writable guest memory. Shared
# adapters using other encodings remain rejected before module generation.
#
# Applies after wasmtime-shared-base-mirror.patch.
# Validation: 7 component string tests (including shared roundtrips, encoding
# guard and bounds cases), 3 SET lifecycle tests, 2 UTF-8 snapshot unit tests,
# a proxied 5 GiB / four-thread probe, and the real wasm64 + SET RISC Box boot.
